00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:38,439
Just as I thought!

257
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:41,617
That energy steroid you were
taking to make yourself stronger!

258
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:44,240
And the pill from inside the tamate box!

259
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:46,297
They're one and the same, aren't they?

260
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:47,680
Uh, tamate box?

261
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:51,337
A priceless artifact passed
down for generations, Jamal.

262
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:55,300
The pills hidden inside were
highly valuable as well,

263
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:58,167
but ten years ago someone
stole them from us.

264
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:00,784
We failed to catch the culprit.

265
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:05,966
His Majesty was concerned that a scandal
might break out, so we closed the case.

266
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:10,857
Actually, Heart, I think that happened
around the same time you left the army.

267
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:11,770
Interesting.

268
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,097
Of course it was me.

269
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:19,097
Look what's happened to my body!

270
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,557
Need me to spill it out for you?

271
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:23,877
The pills were treasured. Air logs.

272
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:26,597
The truth behind their
purpose, lost long ago.

273
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:29,317
Tales of Their power and
the curse that accompanied

274
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:31,757
them were both passed
down merely as legend.

275
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:34,357
But still enough to make us wary.

276
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:37,677
It would appear that our
discretion was warranted.

277
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:38,590
However

278
00:15:38,673 --> 00:15:42,597
However, the tomate box was carefully
guarded for the safety of our people.

279
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:45,300
This result is truly regrettable.

280
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:50,797
If you had not allowed your judgment to
be clouded by foolish dreams of power,

281
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:54,527
you would not have subjected
yourselves to this terrible fate.

282
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:57,580
Wh-What the hell do you know?

283
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:05,180
In any case, they'll never
get their vengeance now.

284
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:10,317
You'll see the heavens have chosen us to

285
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:12,657
settle the score and
that's just what we'll do.

286
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:15,617
Then we'll not only
wipe out the human race

287
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:19,560
we'll annihilate you
and your entire family!

288
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:24,940
I pity them perhaps I ought
to offer them clemency.

289
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:31,137
You're a disgrace to our
people Fishman Island

290
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:34,097
is healing now the least that you can do.

291
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:36,660
is refrain from speaking.

292
00:16:37,860 --> 00:16:41,360
I don't want the children
hearing your poisonous words.

293
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:46,060
Minister of the Left! Huh?

294
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,920
Baron Tamago and Mr. Pecum's.

295
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:50,825
They're at the sweets factory.

296
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:53,240
They're here to collect for Big Mom.

297
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,480
We can't face them now.

298
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:58,497
We don't have any sweets
for this month's payment.

299
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:00,797
Heart and his lackeys
tore the factory apart.

300
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:03,477
And all the candy we
could salvage was sent to

301
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:05,797
the banquet so the Straw
Hats could enjoy it.

302
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:06,939
What should we do?

303
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:17,920
Something tells me Big Mom of the Four
Imperates won't be satisfied with an apology.

304
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:22,400
That a woman would level an
entire country for sweets.

305
00:17:24,060 --> 00:17:28,140
After much celebration, the
banquet finally comes to an end.

306
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:32,153
They're seriously going to
let us keep all that treasure?

307
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:33,270
Cool!

308
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:35,293
That's pretty generous.

309
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:38,557
Do you think Luffy and the
others are all right, Mommy?

310
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,820
I'm so worried.

311
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:41,260
Eh, they're fine.

312
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:44,740
We're going to be fancy
rich pirates now! Woo!

313
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:50,040
It sounds nice, but something tells me
this is too good to be true. Hey, Usopp!

314
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:52,377
Why don't we go look for
the treasure thief, too?

315
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:53,800
Uh, how about no?

316
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:56,657
I found out that guy's
bounty is over 200 million,

317
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:58,817
so he's not going to be an easy target.

318
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:01,180
Whoa, and mine's only 50 berries.

319
00:18:01,460 --> 00:18:04,520
Hey, Zoro, Sanji, check it out.

320
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:06,388
Easiest treasure hunt ever.

321
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,640
That one punch knocked him out cold.

322
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:10,940
I almost feel bad for him.

323
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:14,341
And he left all this loot
sitting out in the open.

324
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,637
Neptune's going to let us keep all this?

325
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:19,097
I guess he really is as goofy as he looks.

326
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:20,010
Awesome.

327
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,397
How much meat do you think this will buy?

328
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:24,656
I think his body could hold all this.

329
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:27,460
I mean, I know he's made
a sludge. But still.

330
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:35,220
One, two, three.

331
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:40,400
Let's take it back to the palace. How?

332
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,460
We need a flying fish.

333
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:45,240
Which way to town, Zoro? That way.

334
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:47,597
Or we could always run off with the loot.

335
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:48,510
What?

336
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:56,017
Well, minister of the left,
please have mercy, Mr. Peckham.

337
00:18:56,100 --> 00:19:00,688
Heart and his crew attacked the factory,
and now we don't have any candy left.

338
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:03,160
And what makes any of that our problem?

339
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:09,357
You're supposed to pay us some candy each
month in exchange for using Mama's name.

340
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:12,057
Don't tell me you've forgotten
about our little agreement?

341
00:19:12,140 --> 00:19:15,199
And I was planning on taking
some sweets for myself.

342
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:17,640
which means now I'm mad and hungry.

343
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:24,397
We've done business with you for a long
time, so I hate to say this, but...

344
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:28,920
I don't think I need to remind you how
scary Mama can be when she's angry.

345
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,880
She'll kill you!

346
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:34,460
Look at those cute little eyes!

347
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:37,180
You'd better pay up! Right now!

348
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:39,600
What's going on?

349
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:46,460
Hey, this is the candy factory
Papa Goo told me about. Yeah?

350
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:49,397
Hopefully we can find a
flying fish around here.

351
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:52,937
This must be the place where they
make that candy I like so much!

352
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:56,020
Hey, guys, are you going
to give us the grand tour?

353
00:19:56,460 --> 00:19:58,580
Ho, ho, Straw Hat Luffy.

354
00:19:59,020 --> 00:19:59,980
Oh, my God, hi.

355
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:02,089
Like, is the banquet over?

356
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:06,000
Luffy, why is he here? Uh-huh.

357
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,362
Dude, I totally pigged out, too.

358
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:13,324
Fishman Island's got all kinds of delicious
food, but that candy was unbelievable.

359
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:15,840
Oh, my God.

360
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:17,230
What's that?

361
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,357
Whoa, whoa, which day on the empty cave?

362
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:23,520
Don't say anything! Oh!

363
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:26,520
Hey, it's Mr. Catfish! What are you up to?

364
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:27,641
They said candy.

365
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:29,700
Just who is this guy?

366
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:34,650
Huh.

367
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:36,880
That's dry hat Luffy, no doubt about it.

368
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:39,740
He's got no business here.

369
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:41,160
He's a pirate, right?

370
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,737
Well, sorry, you see...

371
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:43,860
Listen here, kid!

372
00:20:44,220 --> 00:20:46,573
Tell me what candy you're talking about!

373
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:49,097
I can explain, Mr. Pickles. Actually...

374
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:50,474
Hey, I don't know you.

375
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:51,894
You're not a fish man.

376
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:53,617
Are you here for sweets, too?

377
00:20:53,700 --> 00:20:55,377
I'm right there with you, buddy.

378
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:57,277
I can't get enough of them, either.

379
00:20:57,360 --> 00:20:58,190
You what?

380
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,900
All right, that's it.

381
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,835
Evaporate to say what I think he said.

382
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:08,420
Well, I assure you there's
an explanation. Awesome.

383
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,544
I've never seen a talking lion.

384
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:11,800
It's no big deal.

385
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:14,820
We have a fluffy animal
guy, too. Ah, kiss!

386
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:16,320
Here comes...

387
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:23,246
Threatening this monsieur will not bring
us any closer to the sweets, mon frere.

388
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,520
The tea party is in four days.

389
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:33,000
Let us try to avoid a Foxy pas.

390
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:37,440
If we have to wait here until
morning, well, c 'est la vie.

391
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:40,580
You're just as weird as
he is. What's your name?

392
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:45,000
Bonjour, enchanté,

393
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:51,500
mes amis Pirates Je Zeus Baron Tamago,
I am pleased to make your acquaintance

394
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:53,210
Tamago?

395
00:21:56,420 --> 00:22:00,320
Oui, take care to remember
my name, s 'il Vice plaît

396
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:06,700
Now, excusez-moi, messieurs

397
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:12,497
Am I to comprend that you have
devoured all the sweets in the factory,

398
00:22:12,580 --> 00:22:13,815
my little bon vivant?

399
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:16,000
Did you get that?

400
00:22:16,120 --> 00:22:17,240
Yep, that was me.

401
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:19,952
I could go for some more right about now.

402
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:23,718
Unfortunately, the candies
have met their denouement.

403
00:22:27,080 --> 00:22:27,910
Attends,

404
00:22:27,993 --> 00:22:31,400
that is the jolly roger of
our boss, Charlotte Lin-Lin,

405
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:34,257
also known as Big Mom
of the Four Emperors.

406
00:22:34,340 --> 00:22:39,680
That symbol indicates that this
island is Mama's territory, d 'accord?

407
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:43,317
You see, mama owns the place.

408
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:46,117
Which means fishman island is
under big mom's protection.

409
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:48,237
That's a nice thing to do!

410
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:50,457
I like your boss already.

411
00:22:50,540 --> 00:22:52,011
Kinda weird name, though.

412
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:54,037
Au contraire, mon ami.

413
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:56,077
This is a business deal.

414
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:57,080
Huh?

415
00:22:57,620 --> 00:23:01,380
We allow them the protection
of our mark And in exchange,

416
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:04,759
they have to pay Mama 10
tons of sweets every month.

417
00:23:05,240 --> 00:23:07,260
That's a lot. Oui, monsieur.

418
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:11,760
There is nothing in this world
Mama loves more than sweets.

419
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:17,013
Mama says sweets from Fishman Island
are like creme de la creme, you know.

420
00:23:17,620 --> 00:23:20,780
Pay up tomorrow, and
we will bid you adieu.

421
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:23,357
I'm sorry, sir, but I told you before.

422
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:26,675
The machinery used to make
the candy was badly damaged.

423
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:29,417
It'll take us at least two
weeks to make the repairs.

424
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:31,460
We won't be ready tomorrow.

425
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:34,740
That is not our problem,
monsieur. Hey, fancy!

426
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,962
Why can't you just wait a while?

427
00:23:37,140 --> 00:23:40,577
Yeah, why doesn't your boss have the
balls to come talk to us himself?

428
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:42,737
He's one of the four emperors, isn't he?

429
00:23:42,820 --> 00:23:43,960
Well, your manners.

430
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:48,177
Our leader happens to be a madame
pirate and a fearsome one at that.

431
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:51,880
That said, I do not think Mama
has the balls. It's a girl?

432
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,553
That's different, then.

433
00:23:54,540 --> 00:23:55,760
I love sweets.

434
00:23:55,980 --> 00:23:57,617
I just can't resist the things.

435
00:23:57,700 --> 00:24:00,053
And I really love men who can make them.

436
00:24:03,040 --> 00:24:06,460
Anyway, what if your boss
lady doesn't get her candy?

437
00:24:07,140 --> 00:24:08,700
In that case...

438
00:24:11,760 --> 00:24:12,590
Fall!

439
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:14,300
The deal is off.

440
00:24:14,860 --> 00:24:17,840
The big mom parrots will attack on Mars.

441
00:24:18,020 --> 00:24:21,680
And you can say so long and
bonsoir to this island miserable.

442
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:25,540
You want to destroy the island?

443
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,260
How crazy can you be?

444
00:24:27,700 --> 00:24:29,957
You can't do that over
some stupid candies.

445
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:31,220
I won't let you.

446
00:24:31,580 --> 00:24:33,639
We just saved this place, you know.

447
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:56,180
You seem so happy, Mama.

448
00:24:57,700 --> 00:25:01,680
Yes, it's only four days
until the tea party.

449
00:25:02,140 --> 00:25:03,980
I can hardly wait.

450
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:12,540
I'll finally be able to taste those
delectable candies from Fishman Island.

451
00:25:12,780 --> 00:25:17,680
I'm so excited my stomach is already
producing all the acid I'll need.

452
00:25:18,220 --> 00:25:21,320
Candy, candy, Fishman Island candy.

453
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:23,837
I see you are all excited too.

454
00:25:23,920 --> 00:25:25,180
Of course, Mama.

455
00:25:25,460 --> 00:25:27,580
That's the best candy there is.

456
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:32,580
Then wait for them in my stomach, because
that's where they're all going to go.

457
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:46,620
Oh, oh, oh, oh,

458
00:25:46,820 --> 00:25:50,197
oh,

459
00:25:50,280 --> 00:25:53,617
oh,

460
00:25:53,700 --> 00:25:57,860
oh.

461
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:02,630
Mama!

462
00:26:03,940 --> 00:26:05,340
I'm home now!

463
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:10,140
Oh, Bobbin, how did your mission go?

464
00:26:10,600 --> 00:26:12,520
I set the whole place on fire!

465
00:26:12,660 --> 00:26:14,800
That's wonderful to hear.

466
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:18,397
That country's baked goods
were the best in the world.

467
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:22,020
I bet it smelled so
delicious as it burned.

468
00:26:23,020 --> 00:26:25,617
It's a shame we had to do it.

469
00:26:25,700 --> 00:26:28,600
But they should have honored our agreement

470
00:26:30,800 --> 00:26:32,320
Can I have a snack?

471
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:36,340
If they can't pay in sweets,
they pay with their lives.

472
00:26:37,060 --> 00:26:40,917
There's one thing I can't
stand, it's a broken promise.

473
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:44,277
That, and bitter candy, of course.

474
00:26:44,360 --> 00:26:49,620
Oh, that reminds me, apparently Fishman
Island can't send their payment right now.

475
00:26:53,220 --> 00:26:55,177
Peckholms just told me all about it.

476
00:26:55,260 --> 00:26:56,966
Should I burn that down, too?

477
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:08,420
I want my Fishman Island sweets!

478
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:11,740
Get those fools on the
Transponder Snail now!

479
00:27:15,780 --> 00:27:18,080
I already told Mama Gah!

480
00:27:18,340 --> 00:27:20,377
She's probably calling in to check on us.

481
00:27:20,460 --> 00:27:21,740
Really? No!

482
00:27:22,140 --> 00:27:23,620
Not Big Mom, she's scary!

483
00:27:37,580 --> 00:27:39,860
You talk to her, Egghead.

484
00:27:40,120 --> 00:27:42,238
She isn't going to like this at all.

485
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:45,760
Yeah, what's up?

486
00:27:51,760 --> 00:27:52,860
Who is this?

487
00:27:53,180 --> 00:27:54,437
It's Big Mom, right?

488
00:27:54,520 --> 00:27:56,780
What are you doing? Stop!

489
00:27:57,220 --> 00:28:00,400
You don't sound like Tamago or Peccoms.

490
00:28:01,020 --> 00:28:02,240
Who is this?

491
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:04,320
My name is Monkey D. Luffy.

492
00:28:04,620 --> 00:28:06,444
Soon to be king of the pirates.

493
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:08,780
Was all that really necessary?

494
00:28:10,120 --> 00:28:11,357
Oh, no, Luffy.

495
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:12,620
Nice going.

496
00:28:14,040 --> 00:28:15,300
Monkey... D?

497
00:28:19,720 --> 00:28:22,220
So you must be Garp's grandson.

498
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:25,360
I remember you, young man.

499
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:30,960
You're the little upstart who
interfered with the war two years ago.

500
00:28:31,280 --> 00:28:32,900
There's no more candy! Huh?

501
00:28:33,060 --> 00:28:34,472
They can't send you any!

502
00:28:34,720 --> 00:28:36,580
So I heard correctly.

503
00:28:36,920 --> 00:28:38,920
They're supposed to have ten tons.

504
00:28:39,460 --> 00:28:40,860
Will I eat it all?

505
00:28:40,980 --> 00:28:42,600
It's gone now! Ah!

506
00:28:56,220 --> 00:29:00,257
Don't you lie to me you stupid child you'd

507
00:29:00,340 --> 00:29:03,046
better not be covering
